Chloe, I'm glad you're still here.

00:24:59.109 --> 00:25:02.109
Yeah, well, overtime really helps me resist all temptation

00:25:02.109 --> 00:25:05.109
to Grace Jimmy's MySpace page.

00:25:05.109 --> 00:25:07.109
What's up?

00:25:07.109 --> 00:25:09.109
The fan stalking Rachel must have seen me catch up.

00:25:09.109 --> 00:25:12.109
that bullet. He's the only one who knew it was real.

00:25:12.109 --> 00:25:14.109
Now he thinks I'm a superhero.

00:25:14.109 --> 00:25:16.109
Oh my God, Clark.

00:25:16.109 --> 00:25:19.109
This guy's blog gets like 10,000 hits a day.

00:25:19.109 --> 00:25:23.109
One post? And all of a sudden, you're everybody's favorite boy wonder.

00:25:23.109 --> 00:25:26.109
Can you track this war angel comic to its owner?

00:25:26.109 --> 00:25:29.109
Be a pretty lame sidekick if I couldn't.

00:25:29.109 --> 00:25:33.109
Okay, when I was scanning all of those blogs, I came across a collector

00:25:33.109 --> 00:25:35.109
who tracks a Warrior Angel comic sales.

00:25:35.109 --> 00:25:42.680
Maybe he's registered this one.

00:25:42.680 --> 00:25:43.680
Here we go. Cosmic Comics.

00:25:43.680 --> 00:25:47.680
Cosmic Comics in Metropolis sold one to a Ben Myers last week.

00:25:47.680 --> 00:25:48.680
815 Vine Street.

00:25:48.680 --> 00:26:08.759
I knew you'd find me.

00:26:08.759 --> 00:26:10.759
Only a real hero would.

00:26:10.759 --> 00:26:17.859
You're the production assistant from the movie.

00:26:17.859 --> 00:26:19.859
Where are you?

00:26:19.859 --> 00:26:21.859
Come on, if I told you that, you'd never let me go.

00:26:21.859 --> 00:26:23.859
You're behind the attacks, aren't you?

00:26:23.859 --> 00:26:26.859
Or your angel was all I had.

00:26:26.859 --> 00:26:29.549
He gave me something to believe.

00:26:29.549 --> 00:26:33.339
It gave me hope.

00:26:33.339 --> 00:26:35.339
Or an angel wouldn't try to kill someone.

00:26:35.339 --> 00:26:37.339
You can't mess with someone's idol.

00:26:37.339 --> 00:26:39.339
That's exactly why nobody believes in heroes.

00:26:39.339 --> 00:26:41.339
anymore.

00:26:41.339 --> 00:26:46.930
Including you, Clark.

00:26:46.930 --> 00:26:47.930
And that's where I come in.

00:26:47.930 --> 00:26:50.930
Just like DeVilicus made Warrior Angels stand up

00:26:50.930 --> 00:26:53.930
and save the world.

00:26:53.930 --> 00:27:28.589
You're alive.

00:27:28.589 --> 00:27:35.809
I never gave up on you.

00:27:35.809 --> 00:27:37.809
Lex, why did you do this?

00:27:37.809 --> 00:27:43.009
I see you've given up on me.

00:27:43.009 --> 00:27:50.539
Don't make you pull the trigger.

00:27:53.940 --> 00:27:54.940
Easy.

00:27:54.940 --> 00:27:58.599
We can't all be heroes, Lex.

00:27:58.599 --> 00:28:01.599
Besides, I read about you, Luther's.

00:28:01.599 --> 00:28:03.599
Lina would rather stick around and have his other wrist broke

00:28:03.599 --> 00:28:05.599
than be saved by you.

00:28:05.599 --> 00:28:14.180
What did that?

00:28:14.180 --> 00:28:47.119
Lana, I'm sorry for what you saw in Clark's loft.

00:28:47.119 --> 00:28:49.119
Rehearsing lines?

00:28:49.119 --> 00:28:55.490
It's in his eyes. You're the center of Clark's universe.

00:28:55.490 --> 00:28:58.490
I've only seen love like that once in my life.

00:28:58.490 --> 00:28:59.490
What happened?

00:28:59.490 --> 00:29:01.490
The director yelled cut.

00:29:01.490 --> 00:29:06.690
Updated call sheets.

00:29:06.690 --> 00:29:08.690
Oh God, I can't escape work for three seconds.

00:29:08.690 --> 00:29:10.690
How did you find me?

00:29:10.690 --> 00:29:11.690
Destiny.

00:29:11.690 --> 00:29:22.210
I'm sorry, Lana.

00:29:22.210 --> 00:29:23.210
But there's a hero living among us.

00:29:23.210 --> 00:29:26.210
There's only one way he'll accept his colleague.

00:29:26.210 --> 00:29:27.210
You need to die.

00:29:27.210 --> 00:29:45.259
What do you mean when you said that he was trying to make you accept your destiny?

00:29:45.259 --> 00:29:48.259
That I was supposed to stand for something greater.

00:29:48.259 --> 00:29:50.259
It was my job to save the world.

00:29:50.259 --> 00:29:54.259
He didn't think organic farmer was a close second?

00:29:54.259 --> 00:29:57.259
This guy's delusional, Chloe. You couldn't possibly agree with him.

00:29:57.259 --> 00:30:04.019
Do you want to cue my editorial or do you want to help me find the guy who's going to out you in front of a thousand people?

00:30:04.019 --> 00:30:06.019
What about his hard drive? It might help.

00:30:06.019 --> 00:30:14.960
I think it's too rational. I mean, if Ben is this fractured, we're going to need to loosen a few screws of our own.

00:30:14.960 --> 00:30:18.960
Approach his next move like someone who's blurred the line between fiction and reality.

00:30:18.960 --> 00:30:20.960
So let's think.

00:30:20.960 --> 00:30:26.960
If I'm Devilicus, what is the worst possible thing I could do to Warrior Angel to make him accept his destiny?

00:30:26.960 --> 00:30:41.410
Ow, the kids!

00:30:44.410 --> 00:30:45.410
Don't you see?

00:30:45.410 --> 00:30:48.410
Clark was made for a greater glory.

00:30:48.410 --> 00:30:52.410
But until he gives up his own desires and focuses on the rest of the world,

00:30:52.410 --> 00:30:54.410
thousands of lives are at stake.

00:30:54.410 --> 00:30:55.410
And mine doesn't matter.

00:30:55.410 --> 00:30:59.980
I know it's not easy being a superhero's girlfriend, Lano.

00:30:59.980 --> 00:31:02.980
But Clark has to face his destiny.

00:31:02.980 --> 00:31:06.980
Alone. And you're standing in the way.

00:31:06.980 --> 00:31:58.829
This is crap.

00:31:58.829 --> 00:32:00.829
Are you reading it upside down?

00:32:00.829 --> 00:32:02.829
Lionel Luther lives.

00:32:02.829 --> 00:32:04.829
And he was found on Luther Corp Land

00:32:04.829 --> 00:32:07.829
that no one in the company claims to have purchased.

00:32:07.829 --> 00:32:10.829
Now, did Lex use my tip to find his father?

00:32:10.829 --> 00:32:12.829
Or has he been keeping him there all this time?

00:32:12.829 --> 00:32:14.829
You went behind my back.

00:32:14.829 --> 00:32:17.829
The rules were stay away from the Luthers.

00:32:17.829 --> 00:32:21.829
Careful Grant, you're starting to sound like you care about me.

00:32:21.829 --> 00:32:24.829
More like annoyed.

00:32:24.829 --> 00:32:27.829
That I'll have to babysit you Friday night.

00:32:27.829 --> 00:32:29.829
The planet's being honored.

00:32:29.829 --> 00:32:31.829
You're going with me to accept.

00:32:31.829 --> 00:32:33.829
Ha! Tempting.

00:32:33.829 --> 00:32:34.829
I take notes and look pretty.

00:32:34.829 --> 00:32:37.829
You get a sit at the bar and schmuse with all the important people.

00:32:37.829 --> 00:32:42.829
I was thinking more along the lines of you getting some face time with the who's who

00:32:42.829 --> 00:32:46.829
Metropolis and rescuing me from some long-winded speeches.

00:32:46.829 --> 00:32:48.829
You're asking me on a date?

00:32:48.829 --> 00:32:50.829
God, no. I'm your boss.

00:32:50.829 --> 00:32:54.829
You know what, that's it. You're fired from being my plus one.

00:32:54.829 --> 00:32:57.829
You can't fire me. I never accepted.

00:32:57.829 --> 00:32:59.829
Here.

00:32:59.829 --> 00:33:04.299
Something tells me you don't want to be scooped again by the ledger.

00:33:04.299 --> 00:33:11.980
For the record, if I had been your plus one,

00:33:11.980 --> 00:33:13.980
you would have been my arm candy.

00:33:13.980 --> 00:33:34.140
Lex told me you're living here now.

00:33:34.140 --> 00:33:39.140
Well, you haven't wasted much time.

00:33:39.140 --> 00:33:42.140
Getting back to your roots, have you?

00:33:42.140 --> 00:33:44.140
Well, I know I heard what happened.

00:33:44.140 --> 00:33:46.140
Are you okay?

00:33:46.140 --> 00:33:54.140
It's hardly reassuring to read your own obituary, but you should know that, I suppose, shouldn't you?

00:33:54.140 --> 00:33:58.140
They said that you were being held captive by a crazy woman.

00:33:58.140 --> 00:34:02.140
Indeed, I was. You.

00:34:02.140 --> 00:34:09.900
I would never be involved in something.

00:34:09.900 --> 00:34:11.900
Something like that.

00:34:11.900 --> 00:34:12.900
Oh, please.

00:34:12.900 --> 00:34:15.900
That line stopped working for you the day you faked your own death.

00:34:15.900 --> 00:34:18.900
Lex filled me in on the details.

00:34:18.900 --> 00:34:21.900
Which leaves only one question unanswered.

00:34:21.900 --> 00:34:23.900
How much does Clark know?

00:34:23.900 --> 00:34:28.900
I'm sure that he's thrilled, that you are alive and well.

00:34:28.900 --> 00:34:32.239
I'm sure that you have managed to convince yourself

00:34:32.239 --> 00:34:36.710
that you did everything for the sake of Clark Kent,

00:34:36.710 --> 00:34:39.710
that your love could protect him half a world away.

00:34:39.710 --> 00:34:43.059
Finding your body and paying your captors seem to be.

00:34:43.059 --> 00:34:48.059
your captor seems rather complicated from a hotel in Shanghai.

00:34:48.059 --> 00:34:54.059
You may have lost the Luther name,

00:34:54.059 --> 00:34:57.059
but it's the Luther instincts that keep those claws of you are sharp.

00:34:57.059 --> 00:35:10.130
Please listen to me.

00:35:10.130 --> 00:35:13.130
You are on the edge of a dangerous precipice.

00:35:13.130 --> 00:35:17.130
You could easily tumble down into someplace very dark

00:35:17.130 --> 00:35:20.130
and very hard to escape.

00:35:20.130 --> 00:35:25.849
I hope you don't plan on spreading these lies to Clark.

00:35:25.849 --> 00:35:35.050
You're not trying to protect Clark.

00:35:35.050 --> 00:35:37.050
This is about retribution.

00:35:37.050 --> 00:35:41.050
Let him go, Lana, before it's too late.

00:35:41.050 --> 00:36:12.489
Lex Luthor.

00:36:12.489 --> 00:36:15.489
What are you doing here?

00:36:15.489 --> 00:36:19.119
I thought you might enjoy this.

00:36:19.119 --> 00:36:24.150
Here.

00:36:24.150 --> 00:36:44.750
These are the rarest oriental comics ever.

00:36:44.750 --> 00:36:47.099
A fortune.

00:36:47.099 --> 00:36:56.679
Why are you giving me this?

00:36:56.679 --> 00:36:59.679
Because I've been known to believe in something after the whole world tells me I'm wrong.

00:36:59.679 --> 00:37:03.340
Devilicus.

00:37:03.340 --> 00:37:05.340
He said that exact line to the president in issue...

00:37:05.340 --> 00:37:06.340
175.

00:37:06.340 --> 00:37:12.539
Ben, they dragged you in here, kicking and screaming.

00:37:12.539 --> 00:37:15.539
because you claim you saw a man with superpower

00:37:15.539 --> 00:37:17.539
swipe a bullet out of thin air.

00:37:17.539 --> 00:37:30.230
I'm here to listen.

00:37:30.230 --> 00:37:32.230
There's nothing to say.

00:37:32.230 --> 00:37:34.230
Here's all in my head.

00:37:34.230 --> 00:38:11.820
Did you ever consider career in acting?

00:38:11.820 --> 00:38:14.820
I wanted to say goodbye.

00:38:14.820 --> 00:38:16.820
But don't worry, I'll be back for the sequel.

00:38:16.820 --> 00:38:18.820
What's this?

00:38:18.820 --> 00:38:22.820
Thanks for showing me Smallville had more to offer than a tax break.

00:38:22.820 --> 00:38:24.820
It's a little something from the movie.

00:38:24.820 --> 00:38:26.820
Every superhero needs one.

00:38:26.820 --> 00:38:27.820
I signed on to war.

00:38:27.820 --> 00:38:31.820
or your angel for publicity and a paycheck.

00:38:31.820 --> 00:38:32.820
But after meeting you,

00:38:32.820 --> 00:38:35.820
I'm starting to believe that heroes really do exist.

00:38:35.820 --> 00:38:44.809
There's something special about this one, Lana.

00:38:44.809 --> 00:38:45.809
Hold on to him.

00:38:45.809 --> 00:38:53.539
I sure hope that comment about a sequel was a joke.

00:38:53.539 --> 00:39:01.400
You okay?

00:39:01.400 --> 00:39:04.400
Just thinking about what Ben said.

00:39:04.400 --> 00:39:05.400
Oh, Lana, don't.

00:39:05.400 --> 00:39:08.400
Ben was a crazy fan.

00:39:08.400 --> 00:39:10.400
You got locked up in Belle Reeve.

00:39:10.400 --> 00:39:12.400
He needed hope.

00:39:12.400 --> 00:39:13.400
And he's not wrong.

00:39:13.400 --> 00:39:14.400
Millions.

00:39:14.400 --> 00:39:16.400
of people look up to Warrior Angel.

00:39:17.400 --> 00:39:20.400
What if those people could look up to you instead?

00:39:20.400 --> 00:39:24.320
Well, I know there's not even a million people in Smallville.

00:39:24.320 --> 00:39:36.510
I just want to grab onto you and never let you go.

00:39:36.510 --> 00:39:40.980
But one day the world will need you more than I do.

00:39:40.980 --> 00:39:42.980
I don't want to be the one holding you here.

00:39:42.980 --> 00:39:54.329
I'm not going anywhere.

00:39:54.329 --> 00:39:57.329
For the first time in my life, I have everything I've ever wanted

00:39:57.329 --> 00:39:59.329
and it's right here on this farm with you.

